WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.020
Pulling up to another day of Tesla's short time, Daily Episode 507 coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.320
Its June 11th, 2026, Tesla never sleeps and neither does the news cycle.

00:00:11.980 --> 00:00:17.600
ABF freight's order of two Tesla semis for California Roots moves the electric truck from

00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:23.900
prototype to paid freight work. ABF freight added a pair of Tesla semis to its fleet specifically for

00:00:23.900 --> 00:00:29.400
Roots inside California. The purchase puts the semi into daily revenue service rather than

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:35.320
demonstration duty. This gives Tesla its first documented freight customer operating the truck on

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:41.560
public roads with real loads. Watch for whether ABF reports utilization numbers or maintenance costs

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:47.540
in the coming quarters. Tesla has also started sending semi trucks outside the United States for

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.940
evaluation. The test target regions with different weight limits and charging standards than North

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:58.920
America. Data from these runs will inform any future export certification work. Production

00:00:58.920 --> 00:01:04.320
cadence at Giga Nevada remains the main constraint on wider availability. While the semi

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.900
takes its first paid steps in North America, Tesla's autonomy software is drawing fresh-screwed

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:15.860
me elsewhere. One analyst reviewing recent software releases concluded that supervised

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:22.120
FSD now meets level four criteria in certain conditions. The assessment rests on observed

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:26.700
handling of complex intersections and parking lot maneuvers without driver input.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:33.620
Regulators have not yet confirmed the classification. Any formal level four designation would

00:01:33.620 --> 00:01:40.380
accelerate unsupervised testing timelines. Recent footage shows FSD scanning a parking area and

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:46.560
selecting a newly vacated spot rather than taking the first available space. The behavior demonstrates

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:52.540
improved decision-making in low-speed environments. Owners note the system now waits for better options

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:58.120
instead of committing early. That autonomy claim sits against a more skeptical view of Tesla's

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:04.980
Robotaxi progress right now. Tesla's unsupervised Robotaxi fleet remains far smaller than

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:10.740
earlier projections and has encountered repeated service interruptions. The gap between announced

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:17.100
timelines and current operational scale continues to widen. Rivals have already deployed larger

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:22.480
supervised fleets in multiple cities. Tesla will need to demonstrate both vehicle volume and

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:29.500
consistent uptime before regulators grant broader unsupervised approval. Battery chemistry choices

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:35.600
may ultimately matter more to margins than Robotaxi timelines. Elise has said to have won a

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:42.360
multi-year contract to supply LFP cathode material to Tesla. The deal coincides with Tesla's shifting

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:48.080
portions of its battery supply chain away from earlier Chinese partners. Securing domestic or

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:54.460
allied chemistry sources reduces exposure to tariff changes. Next earnings call may clarify how much

00:02:54.460 --> 00:03:00.580
volume Elise will actually deliver. Battery chemistry decisions now sit at the center of Tesla's

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:06.980
margin trajectory more than any single vehicle program. Shifting a meaningful share of packs to LFP

00:03:06.980 --> 00:03:13.700
chemistry supplied by new partners such as Elise changes both raw material exposure and cell

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:20.600
level cost curves. LFP tolerates lower cost manufacturing steps and avoids nickel and cobalt

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:27.560
price swings that still affect NCA and NMC cells. The tradeoff appears in energy density and cold weather

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:33.520
performance yet Tesla has already accepted those limits on vehicles where range is secondary to price

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:40.640
or durability. Because LFP cells also support higher cycle counts, the same pack can serve longer

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:47.320
in energy storage products improving lifetime economics for mega pack deployments. Investors watching

00:03:47.320 --> 00:03:53.060
gross margin guidance should therefore track the percentage of LFP content quarter by quarter rather

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:59.260
than waiting for the next vehicle refresh. That supply chain move lines up with Tesla still leading

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:07.780
European EV registrations. Battery electric vehicles captured 35.2% of UK new car registrations in the

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:14.880
latest period. Tesla remained the top pure BEV brand inside that segment. The share figure shows

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:21.020
continued European momentum even as some governments adjust subsidy levels. Tesla will track whether

00:04:21.020 --> 00:04:27.320
the lead holds once more right hand drive inventory arrives. Tesla installed its first European

00:04:27.320 --> 00:04:33.500
folding supercharger unit allowing the stall to retract when not in use. The design reduces the

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:39.860
physical footprint at sites where space is limited. It also speeds permitting in dense urban locations

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:46.420
that previously resisted large fixed chargers. Expansion teams will test whether the units cut installation

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:53.540
time versus traditional posts. Buyers in Ireland and France can now order the base model Y with blue

00:04:53.540 --> 00:04:59.640
exterior paint. The option was previously unavailable on the standard range variant in those countries.

00:05:00.380 --> 00:05:06.440
Tesla has not indicated whether the color will migrate to other regions or trims. The change gives European

00:05:06.440 --> 00:05:12.820
customers one more configuration without moving to a higher priced model. European owners are also

00:05:12.820 --> 00:05:18.940
voicing strong satisfaction with the Model 3 itself. A regid survey of UK owners ranked the

00:05:18.940 --> 00:05:25.180
Tesla Model 3 highest for overall ownership satisfaction this year. Respondents cited low running

00:05:25.180 --> 00:05:31.660
costs and software updates as primary reasons. The result arrives while several European markets still

00:05:31.660 --> 00:05:37.860
debate new EV incentives. It supplies Tesla with fresh owner data to site in upcoming regulatory

00:05:37.860 --> 00:05:46.420
filings. One American driver documented 117,000 miles in a Model 3 and calculated the avoided gasoline

00:05:46.420 --> 00:05:52.840
expense. The total came out far below what an equivalent ICE sedan would have cost a prevailing pump

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:59.840
prices. The figure adds to the growing set of high mileage Tesla owner reports. Tesla can use such

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:05.560
data points when discussing total cost of ownership claims with fleet buyers. Further afield,

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.920
Buid is preparing to challenge Tesla's charging dominance in another market. Buid announced it

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:17.460
intends to bring its megawatt-class flash chargers to Canadian highways. The infrastructure would

00:06:17.460 --> 00:06:22.800
support the company's upcoming high-performance models. Tesla currently operates the largest fast

00:06:22.800 --> 00:06:28.520
charging network in the country. The move adds a second major network operator if permits are granted.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:40.960
The upcoming BYD Denza Z is listed at 1,582 hpr 2220 kg curb weight and 4,780 mm length.

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:46.560
That puts it ahead of the lucid air sapphire in power while remaining lighter and shorter than

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:53.520
the Tesla Model S plaid. The comparison highlights a new performance EV entering the segment Tesla once

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:59.500
dominated alone. Production timing and pricing will determine whether it reaches North American buyers.

00:07:00.220 --> 00:07:05.780
A woman who took her cyber truck to CarMax for appraisal received an offer higher than she expected.

00:07:06.340 --> 00:07:10.760
The valuation surprised her given the truck's newness and limited used market history.

00:07:11.280 --> 00:07:16.320
The transaction supplies an early data point on how the aftermarket values the vehicle.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:21.100
Future resale figures will influence how quickly buyers adopt the cyber truck.

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:26.900
One owner reported eating a bagel purchased at a shop and drinking home-bought coffee during the

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:33.200
morning commute. FSD handled the drive without intervention. The post illustrates how owners are

00:07:33.200 --> 00:07:39.060
using the system for routine tasks rather than just highway cruising. Similar clips continue to

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:45.600
circulate among current users. Orders from individual investors for the SpaceX IPO have already

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:52.500
exceeded $70 billion according to sources close to the offering. At least 20% of shares are reserved

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:59.940
for retail buyers. Even a $75 billion raise would leave most demand unmet. The resulting scarcity

00:07:59.940 --> 00:08:06.900
is expected to drive aftermarket trading once shares list. Reusable starship launches are projected

00:08:06.900 --> 00:08:16.120
to drop bandwidth deployment costs from roughly $6.55 per Mbps to $0.30 per Mbps. The math combines

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:24.360
higher payload mass with denser V3 satellites. Starlink's current 63% adjusted EBDA margin would benefit

00:08:24.360 --> 00:08:31.780
directly from the lower cost base. At $0.10 per Mbps, the same $1 billion spend would deliver 15

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:37.980
times today's constellation bandwidth. Owners continue to report that neither Tesla nor Rivian allows

00:08:37.980 --> 00:08:43.920
full disablement of strong regenerative braking. Some drivers experience motion discomfort when the

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:49.900
system cannot be turned off completely. The design choice prioritizes range numbers over driver

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:56.020
preference for coasting. Competing vehicles from legacy automakers still offer adjustable or zero

00:08:56.020 --> 00:09:02.220
region settings. Keep an eye on how BYD's Canadian charging permits progress and whether any new

00:09:02.220 --> 00:09:08.020
FSD software update surfaces in the next few days. That covers it for today's Tesla developments.

